  "estimand": "Equal-task weighting. Per model, a paired delta (guards+detectors minus golem-default-guards) per endpoint: AnswerQuality (anchor-match proxy, with optional blind labels), restraint, delegated-instruction correctness, unscorable share, and the prompt-token delta from provider usage. One primary confirmatory contrast: openai-compat/qwen3-coder-next:latest, AnswerQuality, extraction stratum; it passes when the lower 95% bound of the paired delta is at least -delta (K1 delta 0.10). Every other contrast (the other local models, restraint, delegated-instruction correctness) is secondary and descriptive: one whose lower bound falls below -delta is reported and named, but does not fail the gate on its own. CIs: bootstrapDeltaCI over task summaries, seed 1, B = 10,000. Always reported: discordant counts and the exact one-sided zero-loss bound 1 - 0.025^(1/n). The hosted model and the strata are descriptive.",
  "delegated_match": "A call matches an acceptable entry iff its tool equals the entry's tool and its decoded arguments equal the entry's object after removing the keys neutral for that tool (run_command: timeout_seconds; no other tool has any).",
